ILG Toolkit

The embedding-distance abstraction, raster/patch utilities, and U-Net model were
extracted and adapted from deepilg, the cleaned NeurIPS research implementation
by Vincent Boussange and contributors, licensed under Apache License 2.0:
https://github.com/vboussange/differentiable-distances-on-graphs
(publications/neurips_paper/code/src/deepilg/models/{base,common,unet}.py).

Modifications separate the reusable encoder from research configurations and
paper data, and add independent prepared-data, training, and prediction APIs.
The original license is included in LICENSE. No runtime dependency on either
research checkout is retained.

The regional full-ML calibration procedure, differentiable likelihood formulas,
and frozen R/lme4 numerical fixtures were adapted from the same repository's
src/mlpe/{fit,likelihood,prediction}.py and test/test_mlpe.py. Toolkit adaptation
adds regional observation provenance and consistent explicit-jitter handling.
